ur covariance matrix is\n\n$$\nΣ=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|Σ|=2\\cdot 10-(-4)\\cdot (-4)=4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this value into our expression for the joint PDF, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi \\sqrt{4}}exp(-\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\mu )^{T}\\,{Σ}^{-1}\\,(x-\\mu )) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }exp(-\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\mu )^{T}\\,{Σ}^{-1}\\,(x-\\mu )).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $k=4\\pi .$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549044 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186548956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549044 #edb/ref 1069 "q-159794" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549044 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549044 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2},{X}_{3}]^{T}$ be a multivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\mu $ and covariance matrix $Σ$ given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the distribution of $Y=-{X}_{1}+3{X}_{2}+2{X}_{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549044 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b7717a0a-c395-5f69-ba3c-1ca2b2b29ed2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549044 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if $X=[{X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{k}]^{T}$ is a multivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\\mu $ and covariance matrix $Σ,$ then the random variable $Y,$ defined as\n\n$$\nY={c}^{T}X={\\sum }_{i=1}^{k}{c}_{i}{X}_{i}\n$$\n\nis a normally distributed random variable, where $c$ is any $k\\times 1$ column vector, and  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E[Y] & ={c}^{T}\\mu , \\\\ Var[Y] & ={c}^{T}Σc.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, since we wish to know the distribution of $Y=-{X}_{1}+3{X}_{2}+2{X}_{3},$ we have \n\n$$\nc=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, for the mean of $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={c}^{T}\\mu  \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}